---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Catalogue API" description="Read bicycle manufacturers, groupsets, components and source references through the public VeloGroupsets API.">
  <article class="wrap max-w-4xl py-14">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight">Catalogue API</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-muted">Read the catalogue as JSON, including model numbers, specifications, weights and source references. Cloudflare serves these generated files without running the application Worker. No account or API key is required.</p>
    <a class="button mt-6 inline-block" href="/openapi.json" download="velogroupsets-openapi.json">Download the OpenAPI 3.1 specification</a>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-medium">Browse the data</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7">Start with the index, download a complete collection, or request one record by its canonical ID. Each collection contains all its records in the same order as the catalogue snapshot.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-5"><pre class="text-sm leading-7"><code>{`GET /api/v1/index.json
GET /api/v1/manufacturers.json
GET /api/v1/groupsets.json
GET /api/v1/components.json
GET /api/v1/components/shimano-rd-r7000-gs.json
GET /api/v1/component-types.json`}</code></pre></div>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-medium">Search and download</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7">Download the complete catalogue for a consistent copy of all records, then search, filter and paginate in your own application. Each groupset has a primary riding category: <code>road</code>, <code>mtb</code>, <code>gravel</code> or <code>track</code>. Components inherit their categories through groupset membership. These static files ignore query strings; adding <code>q</code>, <code>limit</code> or other parameters will return the same complete file.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-5"><pre class="text-sm leading-7"><code>{`const response = await fetch('/api/v1/catalogue.json');
const { data } = await response.json();
const derailleurs = data.components.filter(component =>
  component.groupset_ids.includes('shimano-105-r7000') &&
  component.type === 'rear-derailleur'
);`}</code></pre></div>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-medium">Responses and updates</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7">Records are returned in <code>data</code>, alongside a <code>catalogue_version</code> identifying the snapshot. Unknown weights remain <code>null</code>; a listed weight describes the configuration and evidence in its record.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7">Browsers may reuse a response for five minutes before revalidating. Cloudflare supplies an <code>ETag</code> for conditional requests. When combining files, compare their <code>catalogue_version</code> values or download the complete catalogue to avoid mixing releases.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7">Browser applications on other websites can read this public data. This API covers curated records; accounts, community photos and moderation data use separate services.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
